id: pm-web-resume-packets
title: Resume authorized question changes from an admitted cursor
description: "Compose the existing consented agent context scope with SDK history cursors and pm-context prefix-validated delta semantics, without another context store. The overlap check found core mutation events/cursors, pm-context since and freshness, and pm-web context snapshots/realtime replay; none provides project-authorized question-scoped resume packets."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: authorization,context,resume
created_at: "2026-10-25T05:59:37.169Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T11:27:40.529Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-25T11:27:40.510Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-25T07:06:44.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Offline agents receive every admitted selected-item change once after advancing the returned cursor; access revocation blocks future source reads and purges managed cached packet contents; missing or rewritten cursor history requires reorientation rather than an empty delta; typed SDK and CLI, bounded TOON/JSON, UI, docs, non-git public-tracker measurements, seeded model and interleaving proofs, npm and Bun CI release gates."
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T05:59:39.264Z",codex-agent,"Overlap inspected: core listMutationEvents exposes query-bound SDK cursors; pm-context since uses stream prefix hashes and physical ordinals to detect pruning and backdated appends, but its buildSincePack is not a public barrel export and its disk checkpoints retain unscoped pending context. Reusing that store would violate this feature authorization boundary. Compose SDK history reads with the same prefix-validation semantics and existing consented packet revision/audience, retaining only opaque content-free cursor metadata; no second context store or tracker mutation/import/export path. Selection is explicit publisher-owned item IDs bound to the question revision. Existing context UI supplies invalidation/revalidation and no-store handling."
  "2026-10-25T06:10:12.654Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed AgentContextClient.resume and native read-output CLI command, publisher-selected question items, project/principal/revision-bound encrypted metadata cursors, bounded completeness and missed-event receipts, SDK cursor paging plus exact SDK authoritative-prefix validation, and access checks at every source boundary and immediately before return. No native import/export/sync or shared checkpoint state is introduced. Browser proof passed at 1440 and 390 pixels: baseline/resume parity, copied cursor, no overflow, and managed resume DOM purge on revocation. Existing realtime/fallback/backoff revocation cases remain green. Found pinned SDK derived-index staleness on same-size history rewrites; authoritative SDK reads now fence that cache. Host output controls also require read_output registration, now declared for resume."
  "2026-10-25T06:11:09.274Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public tracker measurement passed: 182 certified items; 20 selected streams; 188 admitted events; 394/394 native files byte-identical. Admission 3423 bytes / 494 ms; idle resume 3420 bytes / 359 ms; encrypted metadata cursor 3039 bytes; idle missed=0 and complete=true. Native input files were read-only, with SDK caches isolated in the scratch tracker. The report distinguishes this idle real-data observation from synthetic offline mutation proof."
  "2026-10-25T06:14:15.349Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: disabling pending-row admission makes the offline-resume regression fail (one selected test, one failure); disabling retained-prefix validation makes the history rewrite/gap regression fail with missing expected rejection (one selected test, one failure). Exact source SHA-256 bytes were restored after each control. Targeted production resume/routes coverage measured 98.31% statements/lines, 84.34% branches and 100% functions; the resume service alone measured 99.23% lines and 89.01% branches. Unchanged repository thresholds remain enforced by CI. The first complete seeded run passed all 500 sequences; the linked final run additionally compares every persisted resume-owned context field directly against the reference input via authenticated SDK readback."
  "2026-10-25T06:19:25.562Z",codex-agent,"Final linked validation passed: six resume regressions, zero failures/skips, including all 500 seeded sequences with direct reference-model comparisons of every persisted context field and exact native SDK readback. The companion linked context suite passed 11 tests before the additional scope/budget regression. Deterministic scheduling covers seven named asynchronous boundaries and audience revocation, membership removal, revision replacement, and truthful peer resume (28 competing schedules). Both revert controls failed as intended and restored source bytes. Typecheck, lint, docstrings, zero-duplication, strict tracker health, non-git native JSON/TOON, read-only public-data validation and desktop/mobile browser checks passed. Full npm and Bun release gates are delegated to the unchanged CI matrix on Node 22 and 26 because the shared host is saturated. The implementation is ready for PR review; no merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-25T06:20:46.465Z",codex-agent,"Final interleaving audit expanded the named-boundary check to every boundary occurrence, including the second selected-stream read: nine occurrences times four competing transitions = 36 deterministic schedules. The strengthened regression passed (one selected test, zero failures/skips). This supersedes the earlier 28-schedule count. The final linked six-test run passed with a 600-second runner timeout in 145 seconds, including all 500 model sequences. The initial linked default timeout was infrastructure-only, not an assertion failure. All owned context fields are compared directly with reference inputs read back through the authenticated SDK."
  "2026-10-25T06:31:52.902Z",codex-agent,"Initial Node 26 CI release gate ran 836 tests: 835 passed, with only the pre-existing extension registration count failing because resume adds the thirteenth handler. All resume tests, the 500 seeded sequences and 36 schedules passed in that run. Updated the extension registration contract to advertise resume and its cursor/budget flags; the linked registration suite now passes 12/12, zero failures/skips, and test typecheck passes. CI evidence run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/40168795440 . A fresh complete npm/Bun matrix is required for the corrected head."
